course: dictionary
lesson: 326
title: Angry: a feeling and a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Angry is a feeling. Everyone gets angry sometimes, and that is normal. Your body often shows it, with a hot face, a fast heartbeat or tight fists. Angry can describe a person too: «Jake's dad goes into hospital and Jake is angry at everything.»
explain: What matters is what you do with anger. You can stop, breathe, count to ten, walk away or talk about it. Hitting people or shouting hurtful things is not allowed, because it hurts others. Anger needs a safe way out, such as running, drawing or punching a pillow.
explain: Angry also describes faces, words and stories. «The elder brother, who had stayed at home, was angry that the father celebrated.» The angry feeling changes what the brother does next. When you meet angry in a text, read the words around it to find its meaning.
fact: Angry means feeling strong annoyance or upset because something seems wrong, unfair or hurtful.
fact: Angry can describe a face or words, as in «an angry face» or «angry words».
fact: In stories, angry can describe wild, stormy weather or a rough sea.
fact: A cut or spot that is red and sore can also be called angry.
fact: You can say angry with someone (UK) or angry at someone (US); both are correct.
exercise: «Jake's dad goes into hospital and Jake is angry at everything.» What does angry mean here? | Very happy and calm | *Feeling strong annoyance or upset | Cold and wet | Hungry and tired
exercise: Which choice is a safe way to deal with anger? | Hitting a pillow with your fists and shouting | Saying hurtful things to your sister | Throwing things at a friend | *Taking a deep breath and counting to ten
exercise: «The sea was angry that night.» What does angry mean in this sentence? | Sleepy and slow | Calm and smooth | *Wild and stormy | Warm and sunny
test: Which of these is a sign of anger in your body? | Cold toes | *A hot face and a fast heartbeat | Yawning a lot | Sleepy eyes
test: «She slammed the door angrily.» What does angrily mean? | Very slowly | In a happy way | Very quietly | *In an angry way
exam: People can be angry at the doctors, at God, or at a little sister, and the anger needs a safe way out. What is true? | Hurting people is allowed when you feel angry | *The feeling is allowed, but hurting people is not | Anger is never normal | Only adults are allowed to feel angry
